 # CoopDX Metal Integration Handoff
 
+## Missions 07–08 checkpoint
+
+Current development branch: `mission-07-08-metal-after-dark`, latest commit `b8e4505b9bcfc94039d137cf8aaf99990a4be939`. The working tree is clean. Focused milestones are committed through `ff973f66` (touch UI), `1a4ab8af` (frame-state and cache rewind), `b9c1c755` (Metal upload/sampler hardening), and `abeb3c9d`/`b8e4505b` (touch cancel and ownership tests). This checkout has only the upstream CoopDX remote; do not push mission changes there. The public Apple harness was updated separately under its existing MIT-licensed, independently authored component scope.
+
+Mission 08 is underway: the original iOS control art and layout have been adapted to the shared CoopDX touch overlay, including separate Start and Menu positions, visible C-button priority over the broad camera hit zone, and centered signed joystick-axis mapping. The CoopDX Menu button maps to its regular Start/pause input because it does not expose the original iOS port's separate menu callback. Details and limits are in [TOUCH_UI_PARITY.md](TOUCH_UI_PARITY.md).
+
+The new touch math test passes normally and under ASan/UBSan; `make -j2` passed after the first integration. These tests are being rerun after the latest axis-edge assertions. This is Linux compilation and host logic validation only: no Apple build, iPhone runtime, or visual parity claim is made.
+
+Mission 07 has a first hardening checkpoint: the shared raw/DynOS texture cache now clears all hashmap chains before recycling its bounded pool, and Metal no longer resets cached depth/alpha/decal mirrors at each frame boundary. This prevents stale pool links and frontend/backend state desynchronization. The Objective-C state fix is source-reviewed but not Apple-compiled in this mission. `METAL_STATE_COVERAGE.md` records the full callback matrix and boundaries.
+
+Texture rewind normal and ASan/UBSan tests pass, as do the touch-control tests and Linux `make -j2`. Mission 07 remains in progress: explicit backend texture deletion is still absent, and Metal runtime/DynOS rendering require Apple validation. Existing Mission 06 Apple component validation and full-app blockers below remain unchanged.
+
+The repository's `make test` target is currently blocked because `mupen64plus` is not installed. Focused tests run directly and the full Linux game links. Public Apple component runs [45757822398](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45757822398) and [45758034420](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45758034420) both passed Xcode/iPhoneOS compilation, ARM64 stub-contract linking, SDL layer tests, and generated MSL compilation. The latter includes failure-safe texture replacement and sampler creation. These are not a full-app build or runtime tests.
+
+Touch input also now releases held controls and camera/pinch deltas on SDL focus loss, including hidden chat/player-list controls, so returning from iOS Files or backgrounding should not leave a virtual input latched. Linux compilation passed; UIKit interruption behavior still needs an iPhone test.
+
+Final focused regression pass passed all four scripts, both normally and under ASan/UBSan: combiner shader adapter, SDL Metal layer lifecycle, texture-cache rewind, and touch-control math/hit priority. `make -j2` passed again. `make test` remains blocked by the absent `mupen64plus` binary.
+
