+# Metal Renderer State Coverage
+
+This matrix records the current source-level translation from CoopDX's shared Fast3D renderer into the Metal backend. “Host build” means the Linux CoopDX target compiled; it does not validate Metal API behavior or pixels.
+
+| State / operation | Metal mapping | Coverage and remaining risk |
+|---|---|---|
+| Combiner / shader program | `ColorCombiner` semantic key → generated MSL and cached pair of alpha-off/on pipelines | Key includes combiner values, flags, input mappings, and commands. Linux generator tests and earlier Apple component MSL CI exist; full application ABI and runtime pipeline cache remain unverified. |
+| Alpha blend | `set_use_alpha` selects one of two immutable pipelines | Pipeline cache accounts for blend mode; source-alpha RGB and one/one-minus-source-alpha output. No physical blend-order comparison. |
+| Depth test/write | Four `MTLDepthStencilState` combinations selected at draw | CoopDX booleans are dynamic and applied for each draw. Initial renderer values now match the zero-initialized frontend cache. Frame-local reset was removed because it desynchronized backend state from the frontend's cross-frame cache. |
+| Decal | Per-draw Metal depth bias | Fixed numeric bias is backend-defined; no depth precision or device visual test. |
+| Texture bindings | Both fragment slots are assigned for every draw; absent IDs use the white texture | Prevents stale texture binding leakage. Two texture slots only, matching current adapter. |
+| Sampler/filter/wrap | Two sampler slots, N64 clamp/mirror/repeat mapping; three-point filtering is shader-side | Sampler objects are reused when parameters are unchanged. No pixel comparison on device. |
+| Vertex data | Per-frame bounded shared buffers; explicit generated vertex descriptor | Host stream allocator tests and Apple stub harness previously passed. Dynamic DynOS mesh output has no device validation. |
+| Fog / light map / world color | Generated shader attributes and uniforms | Covered in generated MSL source and previous component compile. Actual scene/color parity remains unverified. |
+| Viewport | Top-left CoopDX coordinates converted to Metal drawable coordinates | Source implementation only; orientation and Retina scale remain device risks. |
+| Scissor | Rectangles are clipped and converted before encoder state update | Pure geometry helper tests pass; actual `MTLScissorRect` execution is unverified. Empty clipped rect suppresses draw submission. |
+| Render pass/depth attachment | Drawable color + per-frame depth texture; color clear and depth clear | Source implementation only. Resize, background/foreground, drawable loss and presentation require Apple app/device tests. |
+| Dynamic textures | Shared 4096-node graphics cache for raw and DynOS resources; Metal texture storage is budgeted | Pool rollover previously rewound position while leaving old hash chains pointing at recycled nodes. Mission 07 now clears every shared chain before pool reuse. Texture object replacement is bounded by cache slots and Metal memory budget; explicit renderer texture deletion is absent from CoopDX's API. |
+| Shutdown | Metal arrays and per-frame resources are nilled; texture byte accounting resets | In-flight completion/shutdown behavior has not run on a Metal device. |
+| OpenGL ES / D3D11 / dummy | Existing backends retain their current API contract | The cache-rewind helper changes only shared cache bookkeeping; backend-specific rendering and fallback behavior are not changed. |
+
+## Fixed state defects
+
+1. **Cross-frame state desynchronization:** `gfx_pc.c` caches depth, depth-write, decal, and alpha values across frames. Metal previously reset its copies at `start_frame`, so a frontend setter could be skipped while Metal used a different value. Metal now initializes to the frontend's initial zero state and retains the mirrored values across frames; depth/decal are still applied per draw.
+2. **Texture-cache pool rollover:** raw and DynOS import paths share a fixed pool and hashmap. On pool exhaustion, both paths reset the pool cursor but previously retained linked hash entries. Recycled nodes could therefore remain reachable from unrelated buckets. A shared rewind helper clears all buckets and resets the cursor while preserving per-slot GPU texture IDs for bounded reuse.
+
+## Validation boundary
+
+`tests/run_gfx_texture_cache_rewind_test.sh` and its ASan/UBSan run cover full-map clearing, cursor reset, retained renderer IDs, and null/empty inputs. A Linux `make -j2` compiles the shared helper and DynOS C++ integration. Public Apple component workflow [45757822398](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45757822398) passed on the iPhoneOS SDK for the Metal Objective-C backend with the frame-state mirror fix (harness commit `a159527c61956337ad27169ce100ca9915cd221e`). Follow-up workflow [45758034420](https://github.com/LawrenceBanes/sm64coopdx-metal-build/actions/runs/45758034420) also passed after safe recycled-texture-slot and sampler failure handling (harness commit `cf84719324268c7129d6b70a858ebcecfbbf7917`). These are component-only stub builds. Complete app linking, GPU/device execution, texture memory behavior under actual mods, and visual parity remain outstanding.
