+# Original iOS Touch UI Parity
+
+## Reference and provenance
+
+The visual and control reference is the original SM64 iOS port in the local Mission 57 worktree. Its landscape UIKit interface uses translucent grey round buttons with dark pressed feedback, a circular joystick base and movable knob, A/B/Z/L/R, C-direction buttons, Start, and Menu. The reference control source credits VDavid003 and explicitly permits reuse in another port when authorship is retained. That attribution is kept in the converted asset directory at `textures/touchcontrols/original_ios/README.md`.
+
+This branch adapts the art to CoopDX's existing SDL/Fast3D touch overlay. It does not modify the reference worktree or copy its UIKit controller, storyboard, or runtime dependencies.
+
+## Mapping
+
+| Original control | CoopDX control | Input mapping |
+|---|---|---|
+| Joystick | `TOUCH_STICK` | Center-relative signed axes, clamped at the base radius |
+| A / B | `TOUCH_A` / `TOUCH_B` | `A_BUTTON` / `B_BUTTON` |
+| Z | `TOUCH_Z` | `Z_TRIG` |
+| L / R | `TOUCH_L` / `TOUCH_R` | `L_TRIG` / `R_TRIG` |
+| Up / Down / Left / Right | `TOUCH_CUP` / `TOUCH_CDOWN` / `TOUCH_CLEFT` / `TOUCH_CRIGHT` | CoopDX C-button bits |
+| Start | `TOUCH_START` | `START_BUTTON` |
+| Menu | `TOUCH_MENU` | `START_BUTTON`, the CoopDX pause/menu input |
+
+CoopDX has no separate `menuButton` callback equivalent to the original iOS port's first-screen callback. Menu therefore enters the CoopDX pause/menu flow through its normal Start input. It remains a separately positioned and configurable control. Additional CoopDX controls remain available in the existing editor and are hidden by default.
+
+The default positions follow the original layout coordinates and edge anchoring. The original circular button and joystick art are converted to RGBA16 assets sized 16x16 and 32x32 for the CoopDX overlay. Controls retain CoopDX's size, opacity, color, position, and reset-to-default settings. Existing saved positions remain intact; fresh configurations use the restored layout.
+
+## Input behavior
+
+- Touch-down chooses one visible control; the broad free-camera pointer region is considered only after visible controls. This fixes the overlap where the camera region captured C-button taps.
+- Each control retains its own touch identifier. Multiple independent fingers can hold movement and buttons simultaneously, and releasing one identifier clears only controls owned by that identifier.
+- SDL focus loss clears all active virtual inputs, slide ownership, camera deltas, and pinch tracking; the release path balances chat/player-list key-up callbacks even if their controls became hidden during the gesture.
+- Joystick displacement is measured around the configured base center, clamped to its radius, and mapped directly into `[-128, 127]`; vertical screen displacement is inverted for N64 stick convention.
+- Existing CoopDX slide-touch behavior remains available.
+- Drawing remains in the shared display-list UI path and does not depend on Metal. OpenGL ES and Metal use the same touch rendering path.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+`tests/run_touchscreen_controls_math_test.sh` covers hit-priority, unavailable controls, separate joystick/button finger ownership, misses, stick clamping, center mapping, signed endpoints, inversion, and integer extremes. The same test is run with ASan/UBSan. `make -j2` validates Linux compilation and linking of the updated controller and generated RGBA16 art.
+
+No iPhone build or physical-device visual/input test has run for this branch. Safe-area placement, orientation changes, apparent scale on current iPhone aspect ratios, haptics, and tactile feel still require device validation. The current shared touch drawing is aspect-aware through CoopDX's viewport and left/right edge anchoring; it has no UIKit safe-area inset source.
